infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Logging call: lazy %s args vs eager f-string
  desc Both render the same line, but only one defers the work until a record actually emits
  compares
    - label Lazy %s args
      children
        - label Level gate runs first, ~100 ns
          desc isEnabledFor checks before any argument is touched
        - label Formats only if the record emits
          desc A disabled level pays nothing past the gate
        - label Message template stays constant
          desc Pipeline groups by shape and graphs a 100x spike
        - label Cheap on the hot path
          desc Millions of calls per hour cost the gate, not a repr
    - label Eager f-string
      children
        - label String built before the call decides
          desc Formatted every time, then maybe discarded
        - label repr of a fat object: micro- to milliseconds
          desc Serialized even while DEBUG is switched off
        - label Silent CPU tax, even when disabled
          desc The three-week hot-path bleed from the Hook
        - label Unique message every call
          desc Kills group-by-template aggregation
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
